V5  THE BUDGET.  From the three inputs
      (L) F_line >= (1/2) lam_line P                    [pincer_line]
      (S) sigma_m(z) >= -C_m Q                          [PILLAR 1]
      (C) |X_{d,j}| <= V_{j,m} n^m P^(m/2) Q^(j/2)      [Lemma CB]
    and the exact identity F = F_line + sum t_m sigma_m(z) + sum t_d X_d
    (verified end to end over QQ by graded_verify_collar.py, quoted):

      F >= (1/2)lam P + (1/2)t_2 Q - [sum t_m C_m + G_2] Q - g_1 sqrt(PQ)
    and AM-GM at alpha = lam/2,
      g_1 sqrt(P) sqrt(Q) <= (lam/4) P + (g_1^2/lam) Q,
    gives the STABILITY form
      F >= (1/4) lam_line P + (1/2) t_2 (1 - Psi*) Q,
      Psi* = (2/t_2)[ sum t_m C_m + G_2 + g_1^2/lam_line ].
    Since ||A - J_n/n||_F^2 = n P + Q, Psi* < 1 gives F > 0 unless
    P = Q = 0.  That is the equality case.

  [ok ] AM-GM step exact over QQ at every sampled (P,Q)
